Models

Voxtral Mini 4B Realtime, by Mistral AI. Apache License 2.0.
  https://huggingface.co/mistralai/Voxtral-Mini-4B-Realtime-2602
  Speakrail adds its own turn-taking head and uses the quantized conversion published by the audio.cpp project.

Gemma 4 E4B, by Google. Apache License 2.0.
  https://huggingface.co/google/gemma-4-E4B-it
  https://ai.google.dev/gemma/docs/gemma_4_license
  Speakrail uses a quantized checkpoint with its own adapter for turn-taking.

Pocket TTS, by Kyutai. Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 (CC-BY-4.0).
  https://huggingface.co/kyutai/pocket-tts
  Speakrail uses the GGUF conversion, with most weights quantized to 8 bits, published by the audio.cpp project.
  https://huggingface.co/audio-cpp/audio.cpp-gguf
